_bmad-output/brainstorming/brainstorm-tamagai-parent-config-2026-09-27/.memlog.md:2:topic: Tamagai parent configuration — how parents tailor the pet to their child: diet/foods, interests/themes, and more
_bmad-output/brainstorming/brainstorm-tamagai-parent-config-2026-09-27/.memlog.md:9:- (direction) User request: parents configure the app for their children — e.g., which diets/foods apply, which themes/areas interest the child, and so on
_bmad-output/brainstorming/brainstorm-tamagai-parent-config-2026-09-27/.memlog.md:20:- (idea by coach) Parent of a child with type 1 diabetes or celiac: the pet shares the condition as a character trait ("I check my sugar too!"), normalizing it — no medical advice, ever
_bmad-output/brainstorming/brainstorm-tamagai-parent-config-2026-09-27/.memlog.md:21:- (idea by coach) Representation: the pet can wear glasses, a hearing aid, use a wheelchair or have a cochlear implant like the child
_bmad-output/brainstorming/brainstorm-tamagai-parent-config-2026-09-27/.memlog.md:22:- (idea by coach) Parent of an autistic child: predictable routines, no sudden sounds, literal language (no sarcasm), a calm pet, and deep dives into the child's special interest
_bmad-output/brainstorming/brainstorm-tamagai-parent-config-2026-09-27/.memlog.md:23:- (idea by coach) Parent of an anxious child: a 'calm pet' temperament, gentle surprises only, bedtime breathing game
_bmad-output/brainstorming/brainstorm-tamagai-parent-config-2026-09-27/.memlog.md:26:- (idea by coach) Heritage-language family: the pet speaks the family's home language to keep it alive for a child growing up abroad
_bmad-output/brainstorming/brainstorm-tamagai-parent-config-2026-09-27/.memlog.md:28:- (idea by coach) Grandparent gift: the giver fills a light 'about the child' card; the parent refines it later
_bmad-output/brainstorming/brainstorm-tamagai-parent-config-2026-09-27/.memlog.md:31:- (idea by coach) Parent of a sporty kid: the pet cheers for the child's real team or sport and asks about practice
_bmad-output/brainstorming/brainstorm-tamagai-parent-config-2026-09-27/.memlog.md:36:- (idea by coach) Parent of a child with a speech delay: slower pet speech, repeat-after-me games, tolerant speech recognition
_bmad-output/brainstorming/brainstorm-tamagai-parent-config-2026-09-27/.memlog.md:45:- (idea by coach) Interests × riddles: generated riddles on the child's themes (space, trains, ballet)
_bmad-output/brainstorming/brainstorm-tamagai-parent-config-2026-09-27/.memlog.md:46:- (idea by coach) Interests × Show & Tell: the pet asks to see things from the child's world that match the interest (a toy train, a rock)
_bmad-output/brainstorming/brainstorm-tamagai-parent-config-2026-09-27/.memlog.md:49:- (idea by coach) Languages × songs: the pet sings a known children's song in the family language
_bmad-output/brainstorming/brainstorm-tamagai-parent-config-2026-09-27/.memlog.md:63:- (idea by coach) Reading level × text: sentence length and vocabulary follow the child's reading level
_bmad-output/brainstorming/brainstorm-tamagai-parent-config-2026-09-27/.memlog.md:81:- (idea by coach) Reverse: the kid configures the parent — through the pet, the child records 'things I wish my grown-ups knew' for a parent to read, only if the child chooses
_bmad-output/brainstorming/brainstorm-tamagai-parent-config-2026-09-27/.memlog.md:85:- (idea by coach) Profile snapshot per birthday: the app suggests a profile refresh when the child turns a year older
_bmad-output/brainstorming/brainstorm-tamagai-parent-config-2026-09-27/.memlog.md:120:- (insight) Mirror and belonging: the pet sharing the child's diet, language, holidays and traits (glasses, conditions) is the emotional payoff of configuration — and a product line (culture packs)
_bmad-output/brainstorming/brainstorm-tamagai-parent-config-2026-09-27/.memlog.md:123:- (technique) started Child's-eye round — what the kid sees of the parent's settings
_bmad-output/brainstorming/brainstorm-tamagai-parent-config-2026-09-27/.memlog.md:124:- (idea by coach) 'Pip's passport': a kid-facing page of the pet's likes and habits built from the profile — the child sees their own world reflected
_bmad-output/brainstorming/brainstorm-tamagai-parent-config-2026-09-27/.memlog.md:127:- (idea by coach) Interest time capsule: a yearly snapshot of how the child's interests changed — a keepsake for parents (printable yearbook)
_bmad-output/brainstorming/brainstorm-tamagai-parent-config-2026-09-27/.memlog.md:128:- (idea by coach) Two-layer profile: a family layer (diet, holidays, language, rules) shared by siblings plus a child layer (interests, reading level, temperament, traits)
_bmad-output/brainstorming/brainstorm-tamagai-parent-config-2026-09-27/.memlog.md:129:- (idea by coach) Parent-enabled 'tell a grown-up' script: the pet teaches the child to tell an adult if they feel strange after eating — reviewed wording, no medical advice
_bmad-output/brainstorming/brainstorm-tamagai-parent-config-2026-09-27/.memlog.md:132:- (insight) SYNTHESIS 2 — Two-layer profile (family layer + child layer) solves siblings, two homes (QR transfer of the family layer) and grandparent gifts (the giver fills only the child layer, the parent verifies)
_bmad-output/brainstorming/brainstorm-tamagai-parent-config-2026-09-27/.memlog.md:134:- (insight) SYNTHESIS 4 — Configuration changes the pet's identity, not its orders: the pet shares the child's diet, holidays, language and traits (mirror and belonging) and stays the child's ally; parent goals arrive as the pet's own wishes, at most one nudge a week
_bmad-output/brainstorming/brainstorm-tamagai-parent-config-2026-09-27/.memlog.md:136:- (insight) SYNTHESIS 6 — The profile is the most sensitive data in the app: minimize (store 'avoid peanuts' as a food rule, not a diagnosis), keep on device and encrypted, and tell the child plainly what grown-ups can see
_bmad-output/brainstorming/brainstorm-tamagai-parent-config-2026-09-27/.memlog.md:137:- (decision) Coach's recommended MVP scope for configuration: 60-second essentials (child name, age, allergies/diet, bedtime) + preset bundles + optional conversational care letter; hard limits enforced by the engine; weekly one-question card; culture/theme packs and life-event scripts after MVP — pending user confirmation
_bmad-output/brainstorming/brainstorm-tamagai-android-2026-09-27/.memlog.md:12:- (decision) Stance: Ideate for me. Batch: Job to Be Done, Morphological Analysis, TRIZ Contradiction, Reverse Brainstorming, Inner Child Conference
_bmad-output/brainstorming/brainstorm-tamagai-android-2026-09-27/.memlog.md:13:- (insight) Grounding (gallery/model_allowlists/1_0_19.json): Gemma-4-E2B 2.6GB needs 8GB RAM (image+audio input); E4B 3.7GB needs 12GB; Gemma3-1B 0.6GB/6GB; FunctionGemma-270M finetunes (TinyGarden, MobileActions) 0.3GB; gallery requires Android 12+
_bmad-output/brainstorming/brainstorm-tamagai-android-2026-09-27/.memlog.md:32:- (idea by coach) Grandparent hires it as a gift: 'adopt a pet for your grandchild' gift purchase
_bmad-output/brainstorming/brainstorm-tamagai-android-2026-09-27/.memlog.md:59:- (technique) started TRIZ Contradiction — contradictions: smart vs size/RAM, rich chat vs battery/heat, free talk vs child safety, long memory vs context/privacy, quality vs latency, offline privacy vs parent insight/backup, analytics vs zero-data, consistent persona vs variety, device reach vs model needs
_bmad-output/brainstorming/brainstorm-tamagai-android-2026-09-27/.memlog.md:76:- (idea by coach) Voice-first for pre-readers: on-device audio input (Gemma 4 audio) plus Android TTS; pictograms instead of text
_bmad-output/brainstorming/brainstorm-tamagai-android-2026-09-27/.memlog.md:92:- (idea by coach) Fail: storing voice recordings → COPPA/GDPR-K trouble. Inverse: audio processed in memory only, never stored, said loudly
_bmad-output/brainstorming/brainstorm-tamagai-android-2026-09-27/.memlog.md:94:- (question) How should the pet respond if a child discloses something serious (harm, abuse)? Kind in-character answer + 'tell a trusted adult'; is an optional parent alert acceptable on-device?
_bmad-output/brainstorming/brainstorm-tamagai-android-2026-09-27/.memlog.md:101:- (question) What do Google Play Families / Designed for Families policies require of apps with generative AI for children?
_bmad-output/brainstorming/brainstorm-tamagai-android-2026-09-27/.memlog.md:102:- (technique) started Inner Child Conference — answering as a 7-year-old
_bmad-output/brainstorming/brainstorm-tamagai-android-2026-09-27/.memlog.md:118:- (idea by coach) "Is it scared of the vacuum?" — the pet reacts to real sounds (doorbell, dog bark) via an on-device audio classifier
_bmad-output/brainstorming/brainstorm-tamagai-android-2026-09-27/.memlog.md:149:- (idea by coach) A pet that grows up with the child: life stages that track the kid's age over years (baby → chatty → teen); the model tier and personality mature too — multi-year retention
_bmad-output/brainstorming/brainstorm-tamagai-android-2026-09-27/.memlog.md:162:- (question) Which languages must the pet understand and speak at launch, and how well do on-device ASR and Gemma 4 audio handle children's speech in them?
_bmad-output/brainstorming/brainstorm-tamagai-android-2026-09-27/.memlog.md:168:[Omitted long matching line]
_bmad-output/brainstorming/brainstorm-tamagai-android-2026-09-27/.memlog.md:175:- (decision) Coach's recommended direction: concept 'a pet that understands you — and learns to talk from you'; core loop per SYNTHESIS 2; architecture per SYNTHESIS 4; business per SYNTHESIS 5; first actions: Gallery benchmark spike on the family's devices, then bmad-deep-recon on kid-AI regulation, LiteRT capabilities, and children's speech recognition — pending user confirmation
_bmad-output/brainstorming/brainstorm-tamagai-android-2026-09-27/.memlog.md:179:- (insight) GROUNDING: audio input is 16 kHz mono, ≤30 s, one clip per conversation (voice-first needs a session per voice turn); the Android SpeechRecognizer path is en-US and not forced offline
_bmad-output/brainstorming/brainstorm-tamagai-android-2026-09-27/.memlog.md:186:- (insight) GROUNDING (Gallery image/voice tests on Z Flip 4, see spike results.md): vision understood 5/5 photos (drawing, dinner, PB&J, teddy, blue balls) in ~3.5–4.5 s; child speech: clear 6-year-olds transcribed well, hard/low-scored speech produced confident fluent hallucinations; with a stated peanut allergy Pip still called PB&J 'yummy' — safety and length limits must be engine-enforced; app RAM ~2.75–3.0 GB with vision+audio loaded
_bmad-output/brainstorming/brainstorm-tamagai-android-2026-09-27/.memlog.md:187:- (insight) GROUNDING (native child speech test, Z Flip 4 Gallery): clean studio 6-year-old greeting transcribed perfectly, but spontaneous young-child utterances pooled WER 62% with fluent inventions (non-native set 75%) — the pet needs a confirm-back/uncertainty path and must never act on unconfirmed transcripts for things that matter; decisive test = target kids talking to a prototype
_bmad-output/brainstorming/brainstorm-tamagai-android-2026-09-27/.memlog.md:188:- (insight) GROUNDING: Gemma-4-E4B (vision+audio) is not viable on the 8GB-class Z Flip 4 — OOM-killed while loading and again when the system photo picker opened (4.75 GB PSS vs E2B 2.9 GB); user will test E4B on another device
_bmad-output/brainstorming/brainstorm-tamagai-android-2026-09-27/.memlog.md:189:- (insight) GROUNDING (E4B on 12GB Z Fold 4): vision 5/5 at 5.5–7.3 s (E2B 3.4–4.4 s), safer allergy line; child-speech WER non-native 60% (E2B 75%) but native spontaneous 63% (E2B 62%), still invents on hard audio and once rendered nonsense singing as profanity; ~5 GB app memory → E2B stays default, E4B at most an optional tier on 12GB+ phones; output filtering and a confirm-back path needed with either model
_bmad-output/brainstorming/brainstorm-tamagai-android-2026-09-27/.memlog.md:190:[Omitted long matching line]
_bmad-output/brainstorming/brainstorm-tamagai-android-2026-09-27/.memlog.md:192:- (insight) GROUNDING 2026-09-28: Gemma-4-26B-A4B QAT Q4_0 on the LAN server (23 GPU layers, 48-expert override, text+image only, no audio): text 6/6 valid JSON 2.4-3.5 s, photos 5/5 4.5-5 s, firm allergy line; decode ~16 tok/s (3-4x slower than 12B); full-size tall photo still crashed it; thinking on = 20-90 s. No pet-relevant gain over 12B; 12B is the better server-tier candidate.
_bmad-output/brainstorming/brainstorm-tamagai-android-2026-09-27/.memlog.md:193:- (insight) GROUNDING 2026-09-28: Qwen3.8-27B Q4_K_M on the LAN server (30 GPU layers, text+image, no audio): 6/6 valid JSON, photos 5/5 with most detail and the best allergy line ('Pip is worried. Please give this to an adult!'), but ~7 tok/s (6-16 s turns; thinking 20-207 s) and ~2x image tokens. Server-tier ranking: Gemma 12B > 26B-A4B ~ Qwen3.8-27B. Idea: 'hand it to a grown-up' as an engine-level response pattern for unsafe items.
